                <pb facs="0583" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2602: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">From Naval Communications for the Information of the
                        Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>U. S. S. “<hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Quincy</hi>,”</placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-08-14">undated</date>.]<lb/>[Received
                        August 14, 1936—10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0014. Following received from reliable eye witnesses: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Evening Tuesday 11th German destroyer <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Leopard</hi> arrived Palma, anchored in bay. Early Wednesday German
                            cargo ship <hi rendition="#italic">Schleswig</hi> arrived and anchored
                            and <hi rendition="#italic">Leopard</hi> moored at mole. An appreciable
                            quantity arms and munitions unloaded, witnessed by local hotel and
                            utilities employees, payment in gold. Also believed modern anti-aircraft
                            machine guns received. Roth vessels departed evening 13th after much
                            fraternization between Germans and local Fascists.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Confirming this report guns using high explosive were noted used against air
                    bombing attack this morning, Friday, for first time.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
